photo-based skin tone classification subject to lighting/quality/rater judgment, mitigated by high inter-rater reliability"}, {"id": 137, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[134, 134]], "note": "caveat that exclusion of players missing photos could bias results if missingness relates to skin tone/outcome"}, {"id": 138, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[135, 135]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 139, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[136, 136]], "note": "5.2 subheading"}, {"id": 140, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[137, 137]], "note": "observational design; cannot rule out unmeasured confounding (playing style, aggressiveness, foul severity)"}, {"id": 141, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[138, 138]], "note": "possible confounding by player behavior/style beyond measured covariates"}, {"id": 142, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[139, 139]], "assertion": "model adjusted for league but did not adjust for individual referee characteristics beyond country-level implicit bias", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["referee characteristics"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 143, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[140, 140]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 144, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[141, 141]], "note": "5.3 subheading"}, {"id": 145, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[142, 142]], "assertion": "red cards are a rare outcome, occurring in only 1.25% of dyads", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["red card outcome"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [146]}, {"id": 146, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[142, 142]], "assertion": "effect size is small in absolute terms (0.18 percentage points)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [145]}, {"id": 147, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[143, 143]], "assertion": "multiple sensitivity analyses were conducted, some of which may be significant by chance", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 148, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[144, 144]], "assertion": "heterogeneity across leagues is strong evidence in Germany/England and absent in France/Spain, so the pooled effect may not be uniformly applicable", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["heterogeneity"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 149, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[145, 145]], "assertion": "discrepancy between RD p=0.020 (bootstrap) and OR p=0.057 (cluster-robust) is due to different inference methods and estimands", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["inference discrepancy"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 150, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[146, 146]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 151, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[147, 147]], "note": "5.4 subheading"}, {"id": 152, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[148, 148]], "assertion": "study is limited to the 2012-2013 season in four European leagues", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["study scope"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 153, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[149, 149]], "assertion": "sample includes male players only", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["study scope"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 154, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[150, 150]], "assertion": "sample includes first divisions only", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["study scope"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 155, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[151, 151]], "note": "may not generalize to other time periods, leagues, or levels of play"}, {"id": 156, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[152, 152]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 157, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[153, 153]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 158, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[154, 154]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 159, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[155, 155]], "note": "section 6 heading"}, {"id": 160, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[156, 156]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 161, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[157, 157]], "note": "6.1 subheading"}, {"id": 162, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[158, 158]], "assertion": "log(games) was used as a continuous predictor", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["log(games)"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [163]}, {"id": 163, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[158, 158]], "assertion": "linearity appeared appropriate based on exploratory analyses", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["linearity assumption"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [162]}, {"id": 164, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[159, 159]], "assertion": "the independence assumption is violated due to clustering (same player with multiple referees, same referee with multiple players)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["independence assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [165]}, {"id": 165, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[159, 159]], "assertion": "clustering was addressed via cluster-robust standard errors", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["cluster-robust standard errors"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [164]}, {"id": 166, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[160, 160]], "assertion": "VIF values were not formally assessed for multicollinearity", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["multicollinearity check"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [167]}, {"id": 167, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[160, 160]], "assertion": "covariates are conceptually distinct and the model converges well", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["model convergence"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [166]}, {"id": 168, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[161, 161]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 169, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[162, 162]], "note": "6.2 subheading"}, {"id": 170, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[163, 163]], "assertion": "1,000 bootstrap replications were used", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["bootstrap replications"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [171]}, {"id": 171, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[163, 163]], "assertion": "all bootstrap replications converged successfully", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["bootstrap convergence"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [170]}, {"id": 172, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[164, 164]], "assertion": "a percentile method was used for bootstrap CIs, assuming the bootstrap distribution approximates the sampling distribution", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["percentile method"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 173, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[165, 165]], "assertion": "resampling was done at the dyad level rather than clustering by player, which may underestimate variance though still valid under mild assumptions", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["bootstrap resampling"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 174, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[166, 166]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 175, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[167, 167]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 176, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[168, 168]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 177, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[169, 169]], "note": "section 7 heading"}, {"id": 178, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[170, 170]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 179, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[171, 171]], "assertion": "overall status is SUPPORTED", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis status"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 180, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[172, 172]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 181, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[173, 173]], "assertion": "the hypothesis that referees give more red cards to dark-skinned players is supported by the data", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 182, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[174, 174]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 183, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[175, 175]], "note": "Primary Evidence subheading"}, {"id": 184, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[176, 176]], "assertion": "adjusted risk difference is 0.18pp (95% CI 0.03 to 0.36, p=0.020)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 185, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[177, 177]], "assertion": "95% CI excludes zero, providing evidence at α=0.05", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confidence interval"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 186, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[178, 178]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 187, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[179, 179]], "note": "Secondary Evidence subheading"}, {"id": 188, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[180, 180]], "assertion": "adjusted odds ratio is 1.16 (95% CI 1.00 to 1.35, p=0.057 with cluster-robust SEs)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 189, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[181, 181]], "assertion": "the CI marginally includes 1.0, but the point estimate and direction support the hypothesis", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["odds ratio CI"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 190, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[182, 182]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 191, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[183, 183]], "note": "Effect Magnitude subheading"}, {"id": 192, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[184, 184]], "assertion": "effect is small in absolute terms, under 0.2pp on a baseline risk of ~1.2%", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect magnitude"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [193]}, {"id": 193, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[184, 184]], "assertion": "given the rarity of red cards and high stakes in soccer, even small systematic differences may be meaningful", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect magnitude"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [192]}, {"id": 194, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[185, 185]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 195, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[186, 186]], "note": "Heterogeneity subheading"}, {"id": 196, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[187, 187]], "assertion": "effect shows substantial variation across leagues, strongest in Germany/England, none in France/Spain", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["heterogeneity"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [197]}, {"id": 197, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[187, 187]], "assertion": "contextual factors (referee training, cultural norms, implicit bias levels) may moderate the relationship", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["moderating factors"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [196]}, {"id": 198, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[188, 188]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 199, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[189, 189]], "note": "Robustness subheading"}, {"id": 200, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[190, 190]], "note": "intro line to robustness list"}, {"id": 201, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[191, 191]], "assertion": "alternative skin tone definitions (very dark vs very light) give OR=1.21, p=0.019", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["alternative skin tone definitions"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 202, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[192, 192]], "assertion": "continuous skin tone measure gives OR per unit=1.27, p=0.012", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["continuous skin tone"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 203, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[193, 193]], "assertion": "controlling for country-level implicit bias gives OR=1.17, p=0.020", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["country-level implicit bias"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 204, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[194, 194]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 205, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[195, 195]], "note": "Caution subheading"}, {"id": 206, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[196, 196]], "note": "observational study cannot establish causality; unmeasured confounding may explain association; small effect and heterogeneity warrant caution"}, {"id": 207, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[197, 197]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 208, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[198, 198]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 209, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[199, 199]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 210, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[200, 200]], "note": "section 8 heading"}, {"id": 211, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[201, 201]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 212, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[202, 202]], "assertion": "analyses were conducted in Python 3.11", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software environment"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 213, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[203, 203]], "assertion": "pandas 2.x was used for data manipulation", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["pandas"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 214, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[204, 204]], "assertion": "statsmodels 0.14 was used for regression modeling", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["statsmodels"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 215, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[205, 205]], "assertion": "numpy/scipy were used for statistical computations", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["numpy", "scipy"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 216, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[206, 206]], "assertion": "matplotlib/seaborn were used for visualization", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["matplotlib", "seaborn"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 217, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[207, 207]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 218, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[208, 208]], "assertion": "full reproducible code was provided in final_analysis.py", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["final_analysis.py"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [219, 220]}, {"id": 219, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[208, 208]], "assertion": "random seed was set to 42 for bootstrap replication", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["random seed"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [218, 220]}, {"id": 220, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[208, 208]], "assertion": "the analysis can be fully reproduced by running the provided command", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [218, 219]}, {"id": 221, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[209, 211]], "note": "code fence with run command"}, {"id": 222, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[212, 212]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 223, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[213, 213]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 224, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[214, 214]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 225, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[215, 217]], "note": "report author, date, and data source metadata"}]}}